# Generated by build.py / the viewers. Nothing here is a source of truth —
# every file is reproducible from build.py plus cem.toml, and several are
# large enough that committing them would dominate this repo's history.

# `bar.sdm` IS checked in. It is the portable artifact this ecosystem trades
# in, and the whole point of the format is that a tool can open one without a
# toolchain: a viewer, an MCP server, or a person reading JSON. Requiring a build
# first would make the example's own subject the one thing you cannot see.
# It rebuilds in ~2 s (`build.py --no-mesh --no-verify`) if it drifts.
#
# Note that a viewer WILL rewrite it in place as you move sliders -- that is
# the rebuild contract working -- so expect it to show up modified after a
# session, and `git checkout` it if you did not mean to keep the change.

# Marching-cubes output — tens of MB each, minutes to regenerate.
*.stl
*.obj
*.ply
*.vdb
manifest.json

# Emitted GLSL + its status journal (sdm-core's glsl CLI, or either viewer).
bar_glsl/
*_glsl/

# Renders. `renders/hero.png` IS checked in -- it is what the README shows and
# reproducing it needs a full 0.2 mm mesh -- so this ignores everything else
# that lands in there rather than blanket-ignoring the folder.
renders/*.png
!renders/hero.png
renders/*.mp4
renders/*.gif
preview.png
preview_solid.png
shader_viewer_envelope.png
*.mp4
*.gif

__pycache__/
